start language dictionary

type:mapping

*-> ""           - included custom string
    -> exm:type="panasonic ats"

*-> about          - about, information about the current context/entity
    -> exm:about:->info

*-> access          - abstract access 
    -> exm:acc:r/w
    -> rule: file:access = false

*-> agent      - mapping operator of AI agent
    -> exm:agent("coder")

*-> alias, assoc      - alias or association of any entity
    exm: [xml,doc,dsl] alias file
           open xml

*-> all          - all, more, everething
    -> exm:all:entries

*-> allow - allow, allowed,
    -> exm:alw:true

*-> any          - any operator of anything: objects, logic, values - the object for everything. `...` is NOT a name of this concept: it is spread notation, it stays text and never compiles
    -> exm:proto(any)
    -> exm:get:dict(any)->show

*-> api             - api/interface logical contract point of any entity
    -> exm:api:->module

*-> autoinc      - autoincrement
    -> exm:autoinc:auto

*-> avt          - avatar, identity surface (person/entity)
    -> exm:avt:source="photo.png"

*-> bct          - breadcrumb, trail of parent contexts
    -> exm:bct: root:sec:item

*-> bdg          - badge, counters/status dot
    -> exm:bdg:count=5

*-> bool          - Y or N - yes, no basic logical boolean
    -> exm:bool:Y

*-> btn          - button action (plain/fab/icon via styp)
    -> exm:btn:name="save" action:apr

*-> business - entity of business logic

*-> cfg             - config/settings file
    -> exm:cfg:settings

*-> char          - char
    -> exm:char[n] - char array unknown size

*-> check - mapping action check/validation
    -> exm: fun "valid file" -> file:check -> return

*-> child       - child dcope of object entity or any unit
    -> exm:chd:->node

*-> cluster      - mapping cluster of any entity

*-> code         - code.
    -> exm:code:java

*-> col          - composition: linear vertical axis of children
    -> exm:col: inp:name="login" | btn:name="save"

*-> complex        - complex
    -> exm:complex:obj

*-> component         - component
    -> exm:component:->code

*-> config - configuration, settings
    -> exm: conf:settings

*-> console      - console, or text visual output
    -> exm:con:out:txt="hi"

*-> content      - content
    -> exm:content:"dictionary"

*-> context - context logical or physical base entity of instance
    -> exm:ctx:proc

*-> controller - entity control manager

*-> convert - convert, rerole, translate
    -> exm:cnv:xml->class

*-> cosine - cosine
    -> exm:cos:deg

*-> crd          - card/surface container
    -> exm:crd:name="user":theme="elevated"

*-> creative, temp - executor freedom scale for the task (0-100): 0 = follow blueprint/spec straight, no improvisation; 50 = own solutions within the structure (names, layout, implementations); 100 = full freedom limited only by syntax and logic. Whole scale: creative=N with N from 0 to 100; 0 (default, if absent) = strict, straight from blueprint/spec; ~50 = own decisions inside the allowed structure; 100 = total freedom, only syntax + logic constrain. Applies ONLY to implementation freedom - never to grammar/dictionary or the given input data. `temp` is the same dial, read as temperature: temp=0.7 means the same freedom point. NOT weight - that is the layout concept; NOT degrees, that is physics
    -> exm:create site:lang=php graphics:lang="javascript":logc={Магазин электротоваров, склад 5 человек}:creative=80
    -> exm:llm:temp=0.7

*-> cxt          - context, execution/working context object
    -> exm:show(cxt)

*-> data         - logical any data
    -> exm: show prj:source:data               command  show me project files content in console
    -> exm: fun:name="convert_to_string" par:name="in" data:type="native" return string        logical multiple data in string data out in implementation on jave or c++ is executed across multiple functions with multiple input parameters num, etc.

*-> date          - mapping date

*-> db           - database
    -> exm:db:sql

*-> def          - default
    -> exm:def:true

*-> dependency - logical dependency of any entity
    -> exm: fun "getData" in data setcall setData
            fun "setData" depend:"getData"

*-> description - description
    -> exm: desc:"what it does"

*-> dict         - dictionary
    -> exm:dict:key

*-> direction     - logical mapping direciton behavior of any entity
    -> exm: card:direction=up to down

*-> directory - directory or subdomain example: dot.comm/project; project is dir
    -> exm:directory:"dot.comm/project"

*-> dlg          - dialog, modal/alert
    -> exm:dlg:name="confirm"

*-> domain          - domain logical language domain
    -> exm: prj:base alias node:domain:root
            crt prj:base

*-> down - direction sign: down

*-> dsl          - VibeDSL
    -> exm:dsl:specfile

*-> dvr          - divider, separator line
    -> exm:dvr:title="section"

*-> endpoint - endpoint logical
    -> exm: endpoint:"/api/v1"

    -> exm:environment:code="PATH"


*-> environment - environment or other variables
*-> error - ERROR AS EVENT: an error occurred; the event is denoted, not raised, and it does not stop the flow by itself
    -> exm:fun event:err:-> return:exception:response

*-> example - example
    -> exm:example:this

*-> exception    - ERROR AS CONTEXT: logical carrier of error information, the error is carried as state, not raised
    -> exm:if(err)->show(excpt)

*-> extend           - extend any entity
    -> exm:extd:key

*-> extension - extension object
    -> exm:extn:extn

*-> fail         - mapping negative or failed action marker
    -> exm: fun:type=rule -> set event:fail->show("im angry")

*-> false, no, N - boolean literal false: synonyms of the bool value N
    -> exm:def:false

*-> file         - file
    -> exm:file:name="out.xml"

*-> flow          - behavior flow of any entity: processing strategy/sequence of an entity (queue, pipeline, etc.)
    -> exm:controller: -> variable:a = list[num]:flow["queue", "pipeline"]

*-> format - format/formatter mapping of any entity
    -> exm: fmt[name,file,date]:table
    -> exm:num:format("0.0")     - float pattern, 0 = digit, 0.0 = 1 decimal, 0.00 = 2 decimals, etc.
    -> exm:num:format("0")       - integer number
    -> exm:num:format("02H")     - hex uppercase, width 2 zero-padded (255 -> "FF")
    -> exm:num:format("0.0%")    - percent, 1 decimal (0.5 -> 50.0%)

*-> framework - framework
    -> exm:frmwrk:name="Hybernate ORM"

*-> frm          - composition: frame, bordered/inset container or viewport crop
    -> exm:frm:image:name="pic1"

*-> fullscreen    - occupy the whole screen

*-> generic      - generic instrustion of current object 
    -> exm: show(file:generic)  - display all:props in file
            show(file:generic)  - display all props, and:props of props, etc.

*-> goal         - mapping positive end action marker 
    -> exm: fun:type=rule -> set event:goal->show("im happy")

*-> graphics, render, visual, UI - UI user interface mapping commands
    -> exm:graph:scene
    -> exm:UI:pan

*-> grd          - composition: grid, two-axis placement (columns/areas)
    -> exm:grd:cols=3: card:name="c1"

*-> grp          - composition: logical cluster of elements, one unit of state
    -> exm:grp:name="form": inp | sel

*-> hint          - placeholder text shown in an empty input field, not a value
    -> exm:inp:name="q":hint="type a command"

*-> hscroll      - horizontal scroll container, base scroll
    -> exm:hscroll: row: card:name="c1"

*-> icn          - icon, pictographic marker
    -> exm:icn:name="gear"

*-> id           - identity of maping in language 
    -> exm:id="goal"

*-> import      - import library, an actual linked artifact. NOT the in operator, NOT in+out: this is ONE word. use() is the internal import, this is the external one
    -> exm:import:frmwrk:name="Hybernate ORM"

*-> in           - input entity or object mapping operator
    -> exm:in:request

*-> incld        - attribute incld="<id>": what is included here. NOT an import - a belonging mark, not an action
    -> exm:incld:->;header

*-> index - indexes or id of physical object or code another lang instruction
    -> exm:open file:"1.cpp" write instr:"case:"index:[0,1,2]->  writed case 1:,case 2: case 3: in cpp file;

*-> infra        - infrastructure, like a router or PC or worker humans or users or datacenter
    -> exm:infr:->node:type="panasonic ats"

*-> inp          - input field (text/number/multiline via styp)
    -> exm:inp:name="login" styp:text

*-> instr         - instruction
    -> exm:instr(obj~obj)

*-> io           - End-to-end any entity state modification without change context, mapping command
    -> exm: fun:name="mapping" param data, param type io(data->cnv(type))

*-> item,node    - logical operator binding a real physical or code object (the concrete item behind a logical node); node - the storage point for that object
    -> exm:rcl:source="items":item="row"
    -> exm:item:name="user_row"
    -> exm:rcl:source="data":node="users"
    -> exm:node:name="users"

*-> landscape - landscape orientation
    -> exm:view landscp:true

*-> lang         - mapping any entity language
    -> exm: prj:lang="c++"
            file:lang="RU"

*-> left - direction sign: left

*-> length, size - length or size of any entity
    -> exm:loop:length:1024 //

*-> lib          - mapping library, codebase, or open source project / git repository, codesnippet
    -> exm:lib:repo="open-utils"

*-> limit          - limit of ane entity
    -> exm:lim:100

*-> line          - logical line
    -> exm:line==row

*-> link         - target affiliation logic instruction. (example link: prj:skl) - command to use skill in project specs
    -> exm:link: prj:skl

*-> list - list/array/collection
    -> exm:list:[v1,v2]

*-> llm, you          - LLM model its you
    -> exm:llm:lng="VibeDSL"

*-> location - logical mapping of location any entity
    -> exm: panel:location=up

*-> logging, logs - logging
    -> exm: convert logs to file

*-> logic        - entity of logic
    -> exm:logic to tree

*-> loop          - repeat cycle of any entity

*-> lowercase - lowercase any text conversacion or mapping
    -> exm: name=lowercase("hello")

*-> map          - logical map/dictionary: key->value pairs of any entity; the default mapping carrier in a task, no separate mapping operator needed

*-> maptree       - mapping tree: e.g. a result as a tree after a query

*-> max          - maximum
    -> exm:max:255

*-> memory - memory
    -> exm:mem:16gb

*-> min          - minimum
    -> exm:min:0

*-> mix          - mix action: combine/merge any two objects
    -> exm:mix:->struct
    -> exm:fun open (file name="out.xml" alias xml ): -> open(file name="project.exe"):alias source:->mix(source *? data:type=dom to xml)->save(file:out_1.xml)

*-> model         - model,  model of any entity or behavior
    -> exm:model:name="user":type="account"

*-> module, class - module, class unit, import type
    -> exm:module:name="kernel.dll"
    -> exm:class:name="user_model"

*-> msg          - message, output/status message object
    -> exm:show(msg(goal))

*-> name         - name of an object, attribute name="<value>"
    -> exm:node:name="out.xml"

*-> nav          - navigation rail/bar/drawer/tab-row, concrete via styp
    -> exm:nav styp:rail: link prj:skl

*-> new          - mapping of creation object
    -> exm:fun:name=i new:txt:          function inner code create a new txt file

*-> null, void, nil - exact empty value (not a logical operator): explicit void, "nothing here" Unlike none (pure logical absence that continues) null is a concrete empty value: where a value is REQUIRED (req/expected), null HALTS the logic - try/catch, fail; none says "not required/absent, keep going"; null says "empty value present, stop here"
    -> exm:fun:name="getarc" if(lng:arc==null)<>:
         -> null
         -> arc
    -> exm:name request -> try:name=="null" cch -> return

*-> num          - unified numeric value for all lang (single representation instead of int, long, float, double): any integer or fractional 32/64 bit number, bit depth and type resolved by value
    -> exm:num:255
    -> exm:num:3.14
    -> exm:num:-42
    -> exm:num:format("0.0") - float format, 0 is a digit placeholder, decimal point sets fraction digits
    -> exm:num:3.14159:format("0.0") - 3.1
    -> exm:num:255:format("02H")     - hex (H), zero-padded width 2: FF
    -> exm:num:255:format("0")       - integer

*-> obj          - abstract definition of object or entity
    -> exm:obj:entity

*-> origin       - original
    -> exm: if syntax is orig ->

*-> os, platform - OS environment

    -> exm:os:win

*-> out          - output mapping of any entity
    -> exm: out:response

*-> ovl          - composition: overlay, layer stacked above the base surface
    -> exm:ovl: dlg:name="confirm"

*-> param - property, parameter
    -> exm:par:name="pic"

*-> parent       - logical property of parent: explicit indication that the value of the property is taken from the parent node
    -> exm:create:fun:type="api":frmwrk=parent

*-> portrait     - portrait orientation
    -> exm:view portrait:true

*-> prg          - progress, busy/loading indicator (linear/circular via styp)
    -> exm:prg 45

*-> print         - mapping operator of visual output logic
    -> exm: graphics type:table event:onCreate->table:print:data

*-> prj          - project
    -> exm:prj:name="picture_lib"

*-> procedure - procedure vertical aligment logical, Unlike a function, there are no input or output parameters; all parameters are drawn from the context.
    -> exm:proc:workflow
           -> var:a = open(file:work)
              a \ {invalid flow if not work}
              var:b = convert a to pdf
           fun "getWorkFlow" in:null out:pdf -> ret workflow:b

*-> prompt        - mapping operator of user/human prompt
    -> exm: prompt:run()

*-> protocol - protocol of any entity
    -> exm: prj:"simple http server" lang:java protocol:http

*-> quote        - mapping of llm text / quote

*-> rag          - Retrieval Augmented Generation
    -> exm:rag:retrieve

*-> ralign        - right aligned layout

*-> rcl          - recycler: first-class virtualized list component, not composed from abstracts; manages its own adapter/view-holder pool, view reuse and lazy data binding via src
    -> exm:rcl:source="items":item="row"
    -> exm:rcl:source="file:list" bind:name/line

*-> reason - reason, syntax example err:rsn="example"
    -> exm:err:reason="example"

*-> ref          - reference mapping of example any entity
    -> exm: file:save(dsl:ref)

*-> required - required, mapping triger to trigger for mandatory parameter entr, none if absent
    -> exm:type: any reqr

*-> response - response logical response of event or action
    -> exm: if(err):response

*-> restriction        - logical mapping of restriction any entity
    -> exm: panel:location=up:restriction=frame:size * 0.25 bhvr:stretch

*-> rgx          - regex
    -> exm:rgx:"^[A-Z][a-z]"

*-> right - direction sign: right
    -> exm: card:direction=up to down

*-> role         - unit role, indicates the role of the entity or object
    -> exm controller:role="cache cleaner"

*-> root         - base scope marker
    -> exm:node=root

*-> row          - composition: linear horizontal axis of children
    -> exm:pan->row: btn:name="ok"

*-> rule         - rule
    -> exm:fun:type=rule:scop=root

*-> scope          - scope of entity 
    -> exm: this:scope = VibeDSL:dict

*-> screen, pag - composition: page, screen or route boundary
    -> exm:pag:name="main"
    -> exm:screen:name="main"

*-> sec          - composition: section, block within a page
    -> exm:sec:name="profile"

*-> sem          - semantic object
    -> exm:sem:syntax

*-> service - mapping service role of entity
    -> exm: thread svc:"micro_transaction"

*-> sht          - sheet, bottom/side panel
    -> exm:sht:name="filters"

*-> single        - single, standalone
    -> exm:single:true

*-> singleton         - singleton
    -> exm:singleton:- class:name="controller" type controller

*-> sinus - sin
    -> exm:sin:rad

*-> skn          - skeleton/shimmer placeholder
    -> exm:skn:name="loading_card"

*-> slr          - slider, continuous value input
    -> exm:slr:name="volume" def 0..100

*-> sort          - sorted mapping of any entity
    -> exm:list[num]:sort:asc
    -> exm:list[num]:sort:desc

*-> source - source
    -> exm:source:file

*-> specfile - mapping of specifics and logic
    -> exm: prj "any" stage:1 create specfile

*-> specs       - specifications of any
    -> exm:file save:data=specfile(dict) lang="VibeDSL"

*-> spr          - composition: spacer, flexible empty space
    -> exm:row: spr | btn

*-> standalone         - stand alone
    -> exm:standalone:true

*-> state        - mapping state of any entity
    -> exm: if(file:state:"opened"):close(file)

*-> static - static, logical static operator of any entity or object implement in code or rule
    -> exm:static:->module

*-> string       - string (var or literal str:"..."; structure is struct, never str)
    -> exm:str:"value"

*-> struct       - any predefined structure or class in the case of OOP
    -> exm:struct:->file

*-> syntax - syntax
    -> exm:syn:"obj~obj"

*-> system - systematization role
    -> exm:system:module

*-> table - table, table mapping of any entity instruction
    -> exm: show(file:"dictionery.txt" to tab:rows["names"])

*-> target      - direct logical indication of a goal: names the entity the task aims at, and nothing else. NOT a result - nothing is produced or returned by it. NOT goal: goal is the marker that the end is here, target is what is being aimed at
    -> exm:target:prj:name="http server"

*-> text         - visual text
    -> exm:text:label

*-> tgl          - binary toggle control
    -> exm:tgl:name="dark_mode" def:dwn

*-> theme - theme visal or logic
    -> exm:theme:dark

*-> think        - mapping operator of model reflections.
    -> exm:think:->show

*-> time          - mapping time

*-> tip          - tooltip, hover help
    -> exm:tip:txt="click to save"

*-> to           - logical pointer from entity to entity read from left to right: maps to the target entity
    -> exm: string to array
    -> exm: file to string
    -> exm: data:"json" convert to data:"xml"

*-> token          - llm token object mapping 
    -> exm: save(llm:token)    example save gurent session

*-> tree         - tree structure of any entity
    -> exm:tree:root

*-> treel         - tree level down
    -> exm:treel:->subtree

*-> treer         - tree level right
    -> exm:treer:->sibling

*-> true, yes, Y - boolean literal true: synonyms of the bool value Y
    -> exm:alw:true

*-> type          - mapping type of any entity
    -> exm: Convert("HelloWorld" lang="ru" type="colloquial")->show()

*-> uid          - unique id like UUID or unique key autoincrement if SQL uuid in program or physical entity 
    -> exm:uid:auto

*-> unique - unique, singlton of any entity
    -> exm:unq:true

*-> unit        - any abstract unit
    -> exm: prj: 
            ->unit:id="router":name="router":model=type {physical router d-link dir 300}
            -> unit:id="o_service":name="service model=type {service of lan packet recursion}"
            -> class:name="route service":type=service:target=router

*-> up - direction sign: up

*-> upercase - upercase any text conversation or mapping
    -> exm: name=uper("HEllO") 
    -> exm: name="Hello world":uper

*-> usr          - language model user, operator.
    -> exm:usr:lang="RU:ru"

*-> valid - valid
    -> exm:valid:ok

*-> view         - concrete view frame: a definite rendered frame/screen instance (not graphics - graphics is the visual element/type abstraction)
    -> exm:view:name="main":source="layout.xml"

*-> vrt          - virtual, logical virtual sequence or entity
    -> exm:vrt:property

*-> vscroll      - vertical scroll container, base scroll
    -> exm:vscroll: list:name="items"

*-> weight        - expand to the full available space, like layout weight 1 in Android

*-> with         - mapping of logic extension
